WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:08.008
[opening theme music playing]

01:02.187 --> 01:05.982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

01:06.941 --> 01:08.568
[man] Can we get more squid soup?

01:08.651 --> 01:10.070
-Okay.
-Okay.

01:10.153 --> 01:12.864
[woman 5] Come here. Get in the net.

01:14.240 --> 01:15.450
Let's go.

01:15.533 --> 01:17.911
-[Sang-gil] Are we reading this or not?
-[child giggling]

01:18.536 --> 01:20.705
-"There was a village…"
-[middle-aged Gwan-sik] Welcome.

01:20.789 --> 01:22.999
-[Hyeon-suk] Come on in.
-[middle-aged Ae-sun] Welcome.

01:23.083 --> 01:24.417
[gentle pop music playing]

01:24.501 --> 01:25.794
Hi, do you have a table for two?

01:25.877 --> 01:27.087
-You'll need to wait.
-Yeah.

01:27.170 --> 01:29.422
-We'll call you back soon.
-Oh, okay, thank you. Bye.

01:31.174 --> 01:32.342
Please wait here.

01:36.971 --> 01:38.681
[man] Guys, I told you, didn't I?

01:38.765 --> 01:42.560
[Geum-myeong] Finally, the bells
began ringing in the middle of the forest.

01:43.394 --> 01:45.605
Along with the sounds of the card machine.

01:46.523 --> 01:49.442
It's all Ae-sun's fault
that I can't retire.

01:49.526 --> 01:51.486
[TV] The uproar about "garbage dumplings"

01:51.569 --> 01:53.196
is affecting handmade
dumpling restaurants.

01:53.279 --> 01:54.489
[woman] It's so good.

01:54.572 --> 01:55.698
It's so delicious.

01:55.782 --> 01:58.827
…because of bird flu. The same phenomenon
is happening to many dumpling…

01:58.910 --> 02:00.662
[Sang-gil] Oh, let me wrap this for you.

02:00.745 --> 02:03.581
I'll make you an amazing seaweed wrap.
Here. Here.

02:03.665 --> 02:05.250
Ah. Oh.

02:05.333 --> 02:07.877
[Hyeon-suk] Stop glaring at the customers
who ask for more soup.

02:07.961 --> 02:10.338
Okay, let's eat this. That and that.

02:10.421 --> 02:12.590
-[Gye-ok] Ae-sun, your daughter-in-law…
-Ah.

02:12.674 --> 02:14.134
I don't want it, Grandpa.

02:14.217 --> 02:15.635
Please eat it for me.

02:16.261 --> 02:17.720
Who will you give it to, Yeong-won?

02:18.304 --> 02:20.682
Your maternal grandpa
or your paternal grandpa?

02:21.182 --> 02:22.892
Ah. Ah.

02:23.935 --> 02:26.229
Ah. No. Oh!

02:26.312 --> 02:27.689
[laughs]

02:27.772 --> 02:30.108
[middle-aged Gwan-sik]
You can't open your mouth and then ask.

02:30.191 --> 02:31.860
Can we get some more squid soup?

02:31.943 --> 02:34.529
-Oh, okay.
-[woman 3] Can we have more soup here?

02:34.612 --> 02:36.364
-[woman 4] Could we also get another?
-[middle-aged Gwan-sik] Yes.

02:36.447 --> 02:40.285
Why are you putting in so much squid?
That's why they eat up everything.

02:40.952 --> 02:44.914
Squid soup needs to be on the menu,
or else you're going to start losing cash.

02:47.876 --> 02:50.628
We need to hire people.
This is too much for you.

02:51.629 --> 02:53.256
Who said it was too much for me?

02:54.799 --> 02:57.677
[Geum-myeong] All that money
made my mom dance.

02:58.178 --> 03:00.555
♪ Singing in the rain ♪

03:01.181 --> 03:02.015
♪ Singing… ♪

03:02.098 --> 03:04.225
Why are you going down
the steps like that?

03:04.309 --> 03:06.269
-[laughs]
-Is menopause over?

03:08.104 --> 03:09.397
No, it's strange.

03:09.480 --> 03:11.608
I'm just in a good mood.

03:11.691 --> 03:15.778
We are making money, Gwan-sik. We're so
busy from early morning to late at night.

03:16.321 --> 03:20.533
But it's not really too tiring
'cause our bank account's growing.

03:20.617 --> 03:22.118
[both laugh]

03:22.202 --> 03:25.371
-You thrilled?
-Yes, I'm so, so thrilled.

03:25.455 --> 03:26.956
Maybe the heavens

03:27.040 --> 03:29.626
have been so stingy all these years

03:29.709 --> 03:31.419
to bless us all at once.

03:32.420 --> 03:34.380
We made a ton of deliveries
during the World Cup.

03:34.464 --> 03:35.924
Jeju has duty-free shops now.

03:36.007 --> 03:38.092
All In was shot in Jeju.

03:38.176 --> 03:39.552
[laughing]

03:39.636 --> 03:42.305
Joonggonara assisted
in getting us Cheol-yong.

03:42.388 --> 03:45.350
Jeong Mi-in did an ad for us.
How is this our life?

03:45.433 --> 03:46.434
[laughs]

03:47.143 --> 03:50.480
Oh, I feel maybe
we're getting paid a reward now.

03:51.522 --> 03:54.776
[chuckles] Honey,
I think we should go on vacations.

03:54.859 --> 03:57.195
Let's go to Guam and China.

03:57.278 --> 03:59.948
If a brat like Mi-suk can go,
then why can't I?

04:00.031 --> 04:01.491
[chuckles]

04:02.283 --> 04:04.911
Why do you always talk
so spitefully of her?

04:04.994 --> 04:06.037
[both laugh]

04:07.789 --> 04:10.416
Oh, if life can continue to be this,

04:10.500 --> 04:13.044
I think I might live
ten thousand years longer.

04:13.127 --> 04:15.129
["Singing in the Rain" playing]

04:16.673 --> 04:19.217
♪ Singing in the rain ♪

04:19.926 --> 04:22.971
♪ Just singing in the rain… ♪

04:23.054 --> 04:27.100
[Geum-myeong] My parents, who once
so diligently dug up a field of stones,

04:27.934 --> 04:30.478
were now people
who had created a landmark.

04:30.561 --> 04:32.981
♪ I'm laughing at clouds ♪

04:33.064 --> 04:36.609
♪ So dark up above ♪

04:37.193 --> 04:39.612
♪ The sun's in my heart ♪

04:39.696 --> 04:43.116
♪ And I'm ready for love ♪

04:43.199 --> 04:46.327
♪ Let the stormy clouds chase ♪

04:47.287 --> 04:49.247
Oh my, my. Mi-suk, that brat!

04:49.330 --> 04:51.958
How dare she call her place
"The Original"!

04:53.209 --> 04:55.169
Do you think you own
all the squids in Jeju?

04:55.253 --> 04:56.671
Did you get a trademark on it?

04:57.255 --> 04:59.132
[Gyeong-ja] What?
Did you apply for a trademark

04:59.215 --> 05:02.010
piggybacking on
someone else's success? Did you?

05:02.719 --> 05:05.555
Hang on.
You come here for another foot massage?

05:06.347 --> 05:08.099
I already said,

05:08.182 --> 05:10.101
yeah, my foot here was asleep.

05:10.184 --> 05:11.102
Why do you care?

05:11.185 --> 05:12.520
You'd better change your sign.

05:12.603 --> 05:13.980
Change your menu!

05:15.523 --> 05:17.900
Leave her alone. I'm grateful for this.

05:19.152 --> 05:21.237
It's better if we compete
for the same thing.

05:25.908 --> 05:27.744
Yeah? Why?

05:28.244 --> 05:32.332
Because with you there pushing fakes,
the real thing sells better.

05:33.458 --> 05:35.460
[jaunty music playing]

05:35.543 --> 05:37.628
[Mi-suk] Uh… [sighs]

05:37.712 --> 05:39.964
[man] Excuse me, can we get
some more squid soup?

05:40.048 --> 05:40.923
Oh, okay, okay.

05:41.883 --> 05:43.843
[Gye-ok] Please sign here.

05:43.926 --> 05:45.970
DDUKBAEGI SQUID SOUP
4,000 WON

05:46.054 --> 05:49.640
[Geum-myeong] But there was someone
who always had a hold over her heart.

05:49.724 --> 05:51.267
Hey, dear.

05:51.351 --> 05:55.730
[Sae-bom] I told you I'd eat it.
I wanted to. I wanted to.

05:55.813 --> 05:58.399
I wanted to. I wanted to. I wanted to.

05:58.483 --> 06:01.069
[Geum-myeong] Yes.
I also had someone like that.

06:01.152 --> 06:02.570
-Momma.
-[Sae-bom] I wanted to do it.

06:02.653 --> 06:03.613
Me, me, me, me.

06:03.696 --> 06:05.656
[Geum-myeong] Even in my terrible 37s…

06:05.740 --> 06:08.326
-[Sae-bom] I wanted to do it!
-…I needed my mom.

06:08.910 --> 06:11.704
[Sae-bom] I wanted to. [sobs]

06:11.788 --> 06:14.874
-[sobs] I wanted to. I wanted to.
-Aw. Okay, okay. There, there.

06:14.957 --> 06:17.335
Come on. I get that she's
in her terrible fours now,

06:17.418 --> 06:20.046
but how can she be mad
that I fed her, you know?

06:20.129 --> 06:23.049
She wanted to eat on her own,
and she's mad that I spoon-fed her.

06:23.674 --> 06:25.218
[panting]

06:27.762 --> 06:29.055
Say "bye-bye" to Mom.

06:29.138 --> 06:31.432
Goodbye! Goodbye!

06:31.516 --> 06:33.184
[Geum-myeong]
I could only see my daughter,

06:33.267 --> 06:34.727
and my mom could only see me.

06:34.811 --> 06:36.562
She lost weight. Even more now.

06:36.646 --> 06:38.356
[Geum-myeong] I'll be back.

06:39.190 --> 06:40.525
Oh, that girl.

06:40.608 --> 06:41.692
She's so shy.

06:41.776 --> 06:43.903
[Geum-myeong] I recognized
a thousand expressions

06:43.986 --> 06:45.154
on my daughter's face,

06:45.238 --> 06:47.698
but I couldn't remember
any of my mother's.

06:49.409 --> 06:51.077
I didn't know it then.

06:51.702 --> 06:54.956
I didn't realize
the only facial expressions I'd remember

06:55.456 --> 06:58.960
were the awkward ones
that she made in photographs.

06:59.043 --> 07:01.045
[gentle music playing]

07:02.713 --> 07:04.257
[nail clippers clicking]

07:05.466 --> 07:07.635
[middle-aged Ae-sun]
Oh, you stubborn child.

07:08.511 --> 07:10.972
Why don't you listen to your mom?

07:12.974 --> 07:15.184
You may be my grandchild, but

07:15.935 --> 07:17.812
but I don't like that you…

07:18.479 --> 07:19.856
you made my…

07:20.648 --> 07:22.108
my daughter suffer.

07:22.191 --> 07:24.694
You may be mean to your mother,

07:26.571 --> 07:28.239
but she's the…

07:30.283 --> 07:32.535
the most important person to me.

07:38.541 --> 07:40.585
Be good to my daughter.

07:42.295 --> 07:43.546
Be good to her

07:44.505 --> 07:46.466
forever and ever.

07:47.049 --> 07:47.967
Okay?

07:49.260 --> 07:50.845
-[door opens]
-[sighs]

07:50.928 --> 07:56.267
♪ Sleep, sleep, sweet child, sleep ♪

07:57.059 --> 08:00.646
♪ My baby is fast asleep ♪

08:00.730 --> 08:04.484
[Geum-myeong] For some reason,
it felt so awkward to simply say,

08:04.567 --> 08:05.693
"Thank you."

08:05.776 --> 08:07.820
Wait, who asked you
to clean the whole place?

08:07.904 --> 08:09.530
And why'd you clean the toilet?

08:10.114 --> 08:11.824
Go rest. You said you're off today.

08:11.908 --> 08:15.328
God, Mom, this is why
I don't want to call you over.

08:15.411 --> 08:19.790
Hey, Miss Terrible Thirty-sevens.
If you're thankful, just say thank you.

08:19.874 --> 08:22.585
I can tell you feel bad
by your… your long face.

08:22.668 --> 08:23.669
[sighs]

08:24.378 --> 08:26.172
-Then set Sae-bom down.
-Hey.

08:26.255 --> 08:29.091
You've been getting cupping
for your back, you said.

08:29.175 --> 08:31.802
[TV playing indistinctly]

08:32.428 --> 08:34.514
[Geum-myeong] Park Sae-bom
is the first person

08:35.097 --> 08:38.768
who's ever made me feel
like I'm completely out of control.

08:39.769 --> 08:41.270
Why is she so stubborn?

08:41.938 --> 08:43.856
She never says yes the first time.

08:45.191 --> 08:47.151
Oh, sweet justice.

08:47.235 --> 08:49.820
Your daughter's just like you. [laughs]

08:51.822 --> 08:52.698
Be honest.

08:53.282 --> 08:54.492
I frustrated you, right?

08:55.451 --> 08:57.578
How did you raise three kids?

08:57.662 --> 09:00.581
Eat the drumstick.
You do what you have to do.

09:00.665 --> 09:01.999
You have to live your own life

09:02.083 --> 09:05.086
so you don't feel resentful
about anything.

09:05.169 --> 09:07.296
Otherwise,
you'll always question your choices

09:07.380 --> 09:08.798
and wonder what could've been.

09:08.881 --> 09:10.258
She will figure that out.

09:10.341 --> 09:13.052
She'll be able to tell
just by looking at you.

09:13.803 --> 09:17.223
Right now,
you're Sae-bom's entire world, you see.

09:21.227 --> 09:22.061
But

09:23.729 --> 09:25.398
that won't last too long.

09:26.566 --> 09:28.568
You won't be a priority.

09:29.485 --> 09:33.197
Later in life,
she won't put you first anyway.

09:34.865 --> 09:36.576
So just do what you want now.

09:37.118 --> 09:37.952
Okay?

09:39.579 --> 09:40.871
[gentle music playing]

09:40.955 --> 09:42.957
Mom, do you regret anything?

09:44.125 --> 09:46.043
Not doing everything you wanted?

09:46.127 --> 09:48.838
[chuckles] No, I wanted to do it all.

09:50.673 --> 09:52.466
Oh Ae-sun, the orphan alone in the world.

09:52.550 --> 09:55.094
Oh Ae-sun the housekeeper.

09:55.177 --> 09:57.388
Dropping out of high school Oh Ae-sun.

09:58.180 --> 10:02.101
The best job I ever had was being
Geum-myeong and Eun-myeong's mother.

10:02.184 --> 10:03.561
I really lived.

10:04.854 --> 10:07.398
I lived life to the fullest in my own way.

10:07.481 --> 10:09.775
Don't look down too much on my life.

10:12.820 --> 10:14.030
Yeah, um,

10:14.822 --> 10:16.824
maybe I'm missing maternal instincts.

10:16.907 --> 10:18.909
Sometimes, I get so angry.

10:21.120 --> 10:22.830
I scream at that girl.

10:22.913 --> 10:24.498
I think I'm losing it.

10:24.999 --> 10:27.877
In the beginning,
no mother knows anything.

10:27.960 --> 10:30.671
Your child will grow,
and then so will you.

10:32.006 --> 10:32.923
[music fades]

10:33.007 --> 10:34.008
Sae-bom,

10:34.091 --> 10:37.011
are you going to chew your food
a hundred times in the morning?

10:37.094 --> 10:39.472
Will you change your clothes ten times?

10:39.555 --> 10:42.725
Why do you give me such
a hard time every morning? Huh?

10:43.601 --> 10:44.435
Why?

10:45.936 --> 10:49.815
If I have an early breakfast,
you leave earlier.

10:50.524 --> 10:53.819
If I eat and finish getting dressed,

10:54.403 --> 10:56.113
you go to work.

10:57.907 --> 10:59.492
Is that why you do that?

11:00.284 --> 11:01.661
So I can't go?

11:02.495 --> 11:03.412
Oh.

11:04.705 --> 11:06.123
I'm sorry

11:06.207 --> 11:09.210
that I yelled at you the other day, okay?

11:09.752 --> 11:10.795
That was my bad.

11:10.878 --> 11:12.755
-[tender music playing]
-Come here.

11:14.131 --> 11:15.424
Oh, you.

11:16.384 --> 11:18.552
Sae-bom, Mommy loves you.

11:19.220 --> 11:22.598
I love you so much, okay? Kisses. Hmm?

11:22.682 --> 11:25.768
[Geum-myeong] A mother's daughter
was now a mother herself.

11:27.269 --> 11:30.231
Mom hoped her daughter's life
with her own little girl

11:30.314 --> 11:31.857
wouldn't be a difficult one.

11:33.025 --> 11:35.444
GEUM-MYEONG: GINGER TEA
SAE-BOM: CHOPPED VEGGIES

11:35.528 --> 11:36.737
CHUNG-SEOP: BLACK GARLIC

11:36.821 --> 11:38.114
My whole life,

11:38.197 --> 11:41.784
my mom never failed to make time for me.

11:47.957 --> 11:50.167
-[Geum-myeong] Honey.
-[Chung-seop] Hmm?

11:50.251 --> 11:53.045
[Geum-myeong] You know the money we saved
to buy Sae-bom a piano?

11:54.046 --> 11:56.382
Can we use that for my parents,
do you think?

11:58.509 --> 12:00.177
I think if I don't do

12:00.678 --> 12:03.431
anything for them, I will regret it later.

12:05.307 --> 12:06.142
Geum-myeong.

12:06.767 --> 12:07.601
Hmm?

12:07.685 --> 12:08.978
Stop, okay?

12:09.562 --> 12:12.773
You don't need to ask.
I'll leave it up to you to make the call.

12:13.524 --> 12:15.109
[moans]

12:17.528 --> 12:20.072
So, should I take my socks off again?

12:20.156 --> 12:22.032
[both laugh]

12:24.493 --> 12:25.995
[bell dings]

12:30.124 --> 12:31.459
So how much is it?

12:33.169 --> 12:35.629
Isn't a Seoul hospital checkup pricier?

12:36.130 --> 12:39.258
You guys would only do this
if I paid for it myself.

12:40.509 --> 12:42.511
Parents still need
to be good to their kids.

12:43.012 --> 12:44.680
Stay healthy for me, okay?

12:44.764 --> 12:46.098
Just a blood test for me.

12:47.057 --> 12:49.643
Come on, Dad,
both knees are totally worn out.

12:50.144 --> 12:52.146
And, Mom, cupping isn't a cure-all.

12:52.229 --> 12:54.190
So what does it come to for both of us?

12:54.273 --> 12:55.775
Just a blood test, all right?

12:55.858 --> 12:57.359
[phone ringing]

12:59.069 --> 13:00.029
[middle-aged Ae-sun] Mm.

13:03.699 --> 13:04.909
Hey, Yong-geon.

13:05.576 --> 13:06.535
I'm in Seoul.

13:07.787 --> 13:09.079
No, I can't come today.

13:10.539 --> 13:11.415
[laughs]

13:11.999 --> 13:13.417
Since we have money now…

13:13.501 --> 13:16.337
-[middle-aged Gwan-sik] Oh, oh, right.
-…he's taking some guitar lessons.

13:16.420 --> 13:17.797
-Acoustic guitar.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

13:18.297 --> 13:19.131
Dad?

13:19.215 --> 13:20.341
-Ah.
-Guitar?

13:20.841 --> 13:22.927
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
Count me out for this lesson.

13:23.010 --> 13:25.471
See, when others got to play it
when they were young,

13:25.554 --> 13:27.973
your father never got to do
anything like that.

13:28.557 --> 13:30.518
Kim Kwang-seok is his amazing new hero.

13:30.601 --> 13:33.479
-Ah, come on.
-[laughs] He has a hobby.

13:34.271 --> 13:35.523
First time in his life.

13:36.023 --> 13:38.025
PRECAUTIONS FOR ENDOSCOPY

13:38.108 --> 13:40.110
[gentle acoustic guitar music playing]

13:45.449 --> 13:47.743
[middle-aged Ae-sun] I told you
we should remove your moles.

13:47.827 --> 13:48.661
You look so…

13:49.453 --> 13:50.955
so tired.

13:52.998 --> 13:54.875
No, what I mean…

13:57.795 --> 13:59.463
I don't wanna go.

14:02.800 --> 14:03.634
What?

14:04.844 --> 14:06.762
Who's telling you to go anywhere?

14:08.222 --> 14:09.765
The thing is…

14:13.185 --> 14:15.688
I can't go build the barrier with you.

14:18.566 --> 14:22.653
I can't go and build the barrier with you.

14:29.451 --> 14:30.286
Dong-myeong.

14:33.038 --> 14:33.998
He can't.

14:36.667 --> 14:37.793
Dong-myeong.

14:40.754 --> 14:41.672
Dong-myeong.

14:44.341 --> 14:45.301
Dong-myeong.

14:47.928 --> 14:49.221
I'm on my way.

14:51.390 --> 14:52.308
Dong-myeong.

14:53.893 --> 14:54.810
Dong-myeong.

14:55.311 --> 14:57.021
[Geum-myeong]
Dad kept calling out his name.

14:57.104 --> 14:58.480
Dong-myeong.

15:00.274 --> 15:04.653
[Geum-myeong] The name that he hadn't
been able to say for so long.

15:05.237 --> 15:07.114
Dong. Dong.

15:07.197 --> 15:08.282
Dong-myeong.

15:08.365 --> 15:10.367
[music continues]

15:14.079 --> 15:15.456
Dong-myeong.

15:15.539 --> 15:17.458
[Geum-myeong] Mom finally got to see

15:18.500 --> 15:21.337
Dad's inner prison for the first time.

15:26.008 --> 15:26.926
[Geum-myeong] Barrier?

15:27.009 --> 15:28.427
ENDOSCOPY CENTER

15:28.510 --> 15:29.678
Yes, he said,

15:30.220 --> 15:31.680
"I shouldn't have gone

15:33.349 --> 15:35.017
to set up the barrier."

15:37.186 --> 15:38.687
"Shouldn't have gone."

15:39.855 --> 15:43.817
He kept saying,
"Dong-myeong, Dong-myeong."

15:44.610 --> 15:45.903
Now I get

15:47.154 --> 15:49.156
why we never talked

15:49.657 --> 15:51.367
about our lost son.

15:55.454 --> 15:57.998
Well, I asked him to tell me
when I was going under,

15:58.082 --> 16:01.001
but before I knew it,
they said I was done.

16:01.085 --> 16:02.711
[both laugh]

16:02.795 --> 16:04.713
Dad, would you like to eat something?

16:04.797 --> 16:05.923
I'll get you anything.

16:06.423 --> 16:08.300
-Pork belly?
-Pork belly?

16:08.384 --> 16:09.927
Yeah. [laughs]

16:10.010 --> 16:11.637
[Geum-myeong] In their hearts…

16:14.890 --> 16:16.433
was a very small

16:18.102 --> 16:19.728
yet massive tomb.

16:33.325 --> 16:35.285
[mimicking engine revving]

16:35.369 --> 16:36.787
[mimicking car horn honking]

16:46.672 --> 16:47.965
You're silly.

16:48.882 --> 16:51.218
Have you been doing that alone
this whole time?

16:52.136 --> 16:53.012
[sighs]

16:55.889 --> 16:58.517
You came today because you thought
I'd come tomorrow, huh?

16:59.018 --> 17:00.477
On his actual birthday.

17:01.520 --> 17:04.440
I followed you because
I knew you were coming here today.

17:06.567 --> 17:10.279
I'm sure Dong-myeong wants to see
his parents on his birthday.

17:12.740 --> 17:14.116
Yes, but it's different.

17:16.076 --> 17:20.330
Families all gather together
at the graves of their parents

17:21.457 --> 17:22.958
but not of their children.

17:23.459 --> 17:24.626
[blows]

17:27.254 --> 17:30.299
I couldn't bear… to see your face.

17:41.101 --> 17:42.186
[sighs]

17:44.104 --> 17:46.899
We can't leave our baby alone. [sobs]

17:48.150 --> 17:50.486
-[wind whistling]
-[sighs]

17:50.569 --> 17:52.571
[emotional music playing]

17:54.406 --> 17:55.449
Oh no.

17:58.327 --> 18:00.537
I'm sure he's scared.

18:02.915 --> 18:04.750
He must be so scared.

18:08.545 --> 18:10.756
[Geum-myeong] Their footsteps
created a path,

18:11.840 --> 18:13.550
and in all four seasons,

18:14.093 --> 18:17.513
the grave where their child lay
was the neatest of all.

18:20.766 --> 18:22.768
[gentle piano music playing]

18:44.748 --> 18:48.502
[Geum-myeong] Dong-myeong's grave
had the most adorable things

18:49.461 --> 18:51.630
that brought them the most pain.

18:52.631 --> 18:54.633
[music soars]

19:09.648 --> 19:10.691
Let's go.

19:15.988 --> 19:17.739
Come back to the house.

19:18.907 --> 19:19.741
Let's go.

19:27.249 --> 19:31.587
[middle-aged Ae-sun] I finally figured out
why we could never talk

19:32.546 --> 19:33.839
about Dong-myeong.

19:41.263 --> 19:44.057
There's no reminiscing
if the guilt is bigger

19:44.683 --> 19:46.268
than your longing feeling.

19:49.354 --> 19:52.441
We adored him because he was the youngest.

19:53.984 --> 19:55.444
He was an angel.

19:55.527 --> 19:57.529
[wistful music playing]

20:00.657 --> 20:04.036
At least we got to hold that angel
for four years.

20:05.621 --> 20:09.041
If I had the choice
to go through it all over again,

20:10.125 --> 20:12.461
I would so that I could hold him.

20:13.378 --> 20:15.464
We'll see him in the next lifetime.

20:16.131 --> 20:17.424
That's getting closer.

20:23.013 --> 20:24.097
I don't want to.

20:24.598 --> 20:27.476
I don't want Dong-myeong
to see me after I die.

20:28.435 --> 20:29.311
Each day,

20:30.687 --> 20:33.482
I pray that my Dong-myeong
would forget about us.

20:34.608 --> 20:36.151
I miss him so much.

20:36.735 --> 20:37.736
Thinking of him

20:39.279 --> 20:40.906
coming to look for us…

20:43.450 --> 20:44.576
It hurts my heart

20:45.911 --> 20:47.746
thinking about how he misses us.

20:48.372 --> 20:49.665
[sobs]

20:59.383 --> 21:00.634
[sniffles]

21:00.717 --> 21:01.885
[music fades]

21:02.886 --> 21:04.805
[middle-aged Gwan-sik]
When are you gonna show me?

21:09.268 --> 21:10.936
What's the title of today's poem?

21:16.650 --> 21:18.902
"The Most Adorable Uncle."

21:19.486 --> 21:20.570
Uncle Dong-myeong.

21:21.571 --> 21:24.992
When our kids told their kids,
"This is Uncle Dong-myeong,"

21:25.826 --> 21:27.536
it was so strange to hear.

21:28.120 --> 21:29.955
And as strange as it was,

21:31.790 --> 21:33.000
I loved it.

21:33.500 --> 21:36.336
Maybe Dong-myeong would feel less lonely.

21:36.878 --> 21:38.046
Oddly enough,

21:38.755 --> 21:39.673
I, uh,

21:40.173 --> 21:42.259
get the feeling I'm less of a bad mother.

21:42.342 --> 21:43.719
[both chuckle]

21:45.137 --> 21:49.016
Listen, how could you be
a bad mother in any case?

21:49.099 --> 21:52.394
-[phone ringing]
-A dog sires a dog. A cow sires a cow.

21:52.477 --> 21:54.354
-[Eun-myeong] Hello?
-Who would sire an angel?

21:54.438 --> 21:56.523
-[Eun-myeong] Hey, yeah.
-Dong-myeong was our angel.

21:56.606 --> 21:57.649
[Eun-myeong] Okay, hang on.

21:57.733 --> 21:59.151
Every night, I stare at your back

21:59.234 --> 22:01.361
while you're sleeping quietly
and dreaming.

22:01.862 --> 22:06.783
I can't sleep because
I find myself staring at your wings.

22:09.119 --> 22:12.581
Hey, Dad, the star of the family
wants to talk to you.

22:13.123 --> 22:15.459
Not Mom? Me? It's me she wants?

22:15.542 --> 22:17.586
Wake up the kids. Let's go home.

22:17.669 --> 22:19.671
[TV playing indistinctly]

22:23.050 --> 22:23.925
Hey, Geum-myeong.

22:24.760 --> 22:26.803
What, will she be in the papers again?

22:26.887 --> 22:28.305
Mom? She's right here.

22:29.139 --> 22:30.724
I thought you wanted to talk to me.

22:31.975 --> 22:34.478
-Yeah.
-She wants to talk to me, right?

22:37.147 --> 22:37.981
Uh-huh.

22:43.236 --> 22:45.655
-[middle-aged Ae-sun] What is it?
-[middle-aged Gwan-sik] Yeah.

22:46.448 --> 22:50.952
[Geum-myeong] Just as things start
to look up, life throws another curveball.

22:51.703 --> 22:53.163
[middle-aged Gwan-sik] Really?

22:54.081 --> 22:55.415
[middle-aged Ae-sun] What is it?

22:55.499 --> 22:58.377
[Geum-myeong] As if someone
was collecting an unknown debt,

22:58.877 --> 23:01.088
there was a voice from the heavens saying,

23:01.713 --> 23:03.006
"I'm sorry."

23:03.715 --> 23:04.716
"I'm sorry."

23:05.384 --> 23:06.843
They just wanna take a second look.

23:07.844 --> 23:09.471
I'm sure it's nothing.

23:09.554 --> 23:12.724
Even if it is something, they can treat
most things now. It'll be fine.

23:12.808 --> 23:14.434
[nurse] Mr. Yang Gwan-sik.

23:14.518 --> 23:16.645
-Yes, yes.
-Please wait at blood testing.

23:18.438 --> 23:19.981
What is going on here?

23:21.149 --> 23:22.901
Why is the Steelheart suffering?

23:24.611 --> 23:25.946
-[groans]
-Dad.

23:27.114 --> 23:28.532
Don't be afraid.

23:29.199 --> 23:30.158
I've got your back.

23:30.242 --> 23:32.452
I'll be right here with you, okay?

23:34.329 --> 23:36.706
I'm not. I don't feel worried.

23:37.541 --> 23:38.750
I know my own body.

23:41.670 --> 23:43.463
[Geum-myeong] But no one knew

23:43.547 --> 23:44.965
just how very,

23:45.632 --> 23:46.883
very weak

23:47.801 --> 23:49.970
the Steelheart had become.

23:50.053 --> 23:52.055
[gentle acoustic guitar music playing]

23:53.890 --> 23:55.016
[Geum-myeong sighs]

23:56.476 --> 23:58.437
-Look, um…
-Mm.

23:59.271 --> 24:01.648
Don't cry, no matter what
the doctors might say.

24:02.732 --> 24:05.444
[middle-aged Ae-sun] Not your dad.
He doesn't deserve it.

24:05.944 --> 24:08.405
There's no one in the world
as kind as your dad.

24:09.448 --> 24:10.824
Hey, Mom. Mom.

24:11.825 --> 24:12.659
Did you hear me?

24:13.326 --> 24:15.120
No matter how sick he may be,

24:15.704 --> 24:17.289
I'll make sure he gets treated.

24:17.914 --> 24:19.291
Yeah, I believe you.

24:19.875 --> 24:21.209
I believe you.

24:21.293 --> 24:22.919
[Geum-myeong] So don't cry
in front of Dad.

24:25.172 --> 24:27.007
He's feeling a bit of a shock right now.

24:30.594 --> 24:33.346
[doctor] You've had rheumatoid arthritis
for a long time.

24:33.847 --> 24:36.349
I don't know how you bore
so much pain for so long.

24:37.058 --> 24:39.686
Sometimes, the symptoms of
multiple myeloma are mistaken

24:39.769 --> 24:41.605
for rheumatoid arthritis in joints,

24:42.147 --> 24:44.357
which can delay a correct diagnosis.

24:44.941 --> 24:46.485
Multiple myeloma

24:47.194 --> 24:48.612
is a kind of blood cancer.

24:48.695 --> 24:51.448
Let's call it
a distant relative of leukemia.

24:52.032 --> 24:54.659
[Geum-myeong] He never knew anything
about pop culture.

24:54.743 --> 24:56.995
I was always frustrated with Dad because

24:57.078 --> 25:00.499
every time there was a new girl band,
he'd ask, "Is that Sung Yu-ri?"

25:01.041 --> 25:03.793
Dad just wanted to have
conversations with his daughter.

25:04.961 --> 25:07.005
He also wanted to play the guitar.

25:07.881 --> 25:11.092
But I didn't understand,
or I pretended not to.

25:11.176 --> 25:12.677
People who just bear the pain

25:12.761 --> 25:15.096
actually permit the disease
to develop further.

25:15.597 --> 25:19.351
This has already progressed
to kidney failure, and you didn't know it.

25:19.434 --> 25:21.645
You must've been very tired all the time.

25:22.229 --> 25:23.230
So…

25:25.941 --> 25:26.816
what now?

25:28.652 --> 25:29.736
Well, at this point,

25:30.695 --> 25:32.489
if we start the treatment now,

25:33.406 --> 25:34.908
he could have a slight chance.

25:36.535 --> 25:37.536
But that's about it.

25:38.662 --> 25:39.871
[Geum-myeong sobs]

25:41.915 --> 25:44.459
[Geum-myeong] The heavens
were merciless to my dad,

25:45.627 --> 25:48.505
who had just become interested
in Kim Kwang-seok.

25:51.466 --> 25:53.093
[middle-aged Ae-sun] Yeah, yeah.

25:53.802 --> 25:55.595
Uh, you don't need to pick him up.

25:56.263 --> 25:59.599
Geum-myeong, he'll be at the hospital
longer than one or two days.

25:59.683 --> 26:00.809
Don't do that.

26:00.892 --> 26:03.645
It'll be too much. Too much for you.

26:03.728 --> 26:05.730
[wind whistling]

26:19.869 --> 26:20.704
[sighs]

26:23.039 --> 26:23.873
Here.

26:28.211 --> 26:29.713
Don't you worry about it.

26:30.672 --> 26:33.174
We'll get it done.
We'll get what you need.

26:34.301 --> 26:35.802
I'll get the right treatment.

26:37.762 --> 26:38.597
Let's go.

26:39.931 --> 26:40.849
[sighs]

26:45.687 --> 26:47.689
[wistful music playing]

26:54.070 --> 26:56.615
[Geum-myeong] The 24 sessions
of chemotherapy

26:57.240 --> 26:58.825
melted the Steelheart.

26:59.451 --> 27:01.870
Mom even forgot which season it was.

27:02.871 --> 27:06.207
Hey, my angel. Look at the flowers.

27:08.877 --> 27:11.254
Writing poems, you need to enjoy nature.

27:12.213 --> 27:13.340
Have you been writing?

27:14.758 --> 27:16.551
I wanna read your poems.

27:17.886 --> 27:20.847
You love flowers so much,
but you're staring at my feet.

27:21.348 --> 27:23.933
I can't let you fall.

27:24.893 --> 27:25.810
Have a look.

27:26.645 --> 27:27.646
Look at the flowers.

27:44.579 --> 27:48.041
Next year,
let's see the leaves in Zhangjiajie.

27:48.792 --> 27:51.544
The brat Mi-suk went there.
She was showing off.

27:53.296 --> 27:54.506
[chuckles]

27:54.589 --> 27:56.591
Why are you holding my hands so tightly?

27:57.258 --> 27:59.302
You think someone's taking me away?

27:59.386 --> 28:00.762
If you leave me,

28:01.596 --> 28:02.722
I'll be alone.

28:03.306 --> 28:04.140
You know that?

28:04.224 --> 28:05.934
You'll never be alone. You have our kids.

28:06.017 --> 28:07.268
Oh, but I don't.

28:08.311 --> 28:10.146
They have their own families now.

28:12.315 --> 28:13.817
A big nuisance.

28:14.609 --> 28:16.236
You see yourself as a nuisance.

28:17.278 --> 28:19.364
When we were young, I'd think about

28:19.447 --> 28:21.866
your uncle not letting you
have croakers at home,

28:22.450 --> 28:24.828
and I'd get so angry I wouldn't be able to

28:26.371 --> 28:27.497
sleep at all.

28:28.665 --> 28:31.793
Ever since then,
you've seen yourself as a nuisance.

28:34.629 --> 28:35.797
So you need to win.

28:36.798 --> 28:40.844
A single mother is nothing
but a nuisance to her children.

28:42.470 --> 28:44.264
Don't make me grow old on my own.

28:45.432 --> 28:46.516
Of course.

28:46.599 --> 28:48.143
I'll never leave you.

28:51.354 --> 28:52.313
[sighs]

28:52.397 --> 28:54.858
I wouldn't dare leave
Ae-sun behind all alone.

28:56.276 --> 28:58.236
[Geum-myeong] The rest of my dad's life

28:58.319 --> 29:00.280
passed like a cherry blossom's.

29:04.117 --> 29:08.496
Oh! That was tough, huh?
Did it make you feel queasy?

29:08.580 --> 29:09.581
Not really.

29:09.664 --> 29:11.040
There was no pain.

29:11.124 --> 29:13.168
It was painful. Don't say it wasn't.

29:13.668 --> 29:15.086
Of course it hurt. How could it not?

29:15.170 --> 29:16.337
Is Yang Gwan-sik here?

29:17.088 --> 29:18.089
Oh, yes, yes.

29:19.340 --> 29:21.509
Drink this, okay? Drink it, okay?

29:22.302 --> 29:24.387
-[nurse] Mr. Seo Ji-won.
-Yes.

29:25.847 --> 29:27.390
Did you get the blood work done already?

29:28.183 --> 29:32.103
Oh, no, I was told downstairs
to come here first.

29:32.187 --> 29:34.272
The instructions are written right there.

29:34.856 --> 29:36.232
[middle-aged Ae-sun] Oh my.

29:36.316 --> 29:38.651
-[nurse 2] Please leave.
-[middle-aged Ae-sun] Sorry?

29:38.735 --> 29:40.528
-[nurse 2] Please go out.
-I'm supposed to be…

29:40.612 --> 29:43.698
You can't just walk in.
You have to put those out here. Here.

29:43.782 --> 29:47.076
-Oh, I, um, didn't see…
-It's written right here.

29:49.954 --> 29:51.790
Ms. Park Gyeong-ja. Come in, please.

29:53.541 --> 29:54.626
[chuckles]

29:58.213 --> 30:02.008
Uh, so he can eat meat of any kind?

30:02.592 --> 30:05.678
Someone said it wouldn't actually be
healthy for him to eat it.

30:05.762 --> 30:07.096
Sure, he should eat well.

30:07.180 --> 30:09.349
-Ah.
-[doctor] Then see you next month.

30:09.432 --> 30:12.685
Well, sir, would moxibustion be
a good thing he should get?

30:13.478 --> 30:16.105
I hear moxibustion would be good for him.

30:16.189 --> 30:19.025
[sighs] Will you be asking me about
everything on the Internet?

30:19.526 --> 30:20.360
Uh…

30:27.575 --> 30:31.913
[middle-aged Ae-sun] Is this not it?
I have number 832.

30:32.497 --> 30:34.541
You can't bring the number
for the payment window

30:34.624 --> 30:36.000
to the reception window.

30:37.210 --> 30:39.754
Oh. So this number is…

30:39.838 --> 30:42.715
-[man] It's written right over there.
-Oh, so it's…

30:43.383 --> 30:44.801
[man sighs]

30:47.679 --> 30:49.597
Last call for 835.

30:51.850 --> 30:52.934
Cut us some slack.

30:53.017 --> 30:54.143
Can you, please?

30:55.019 --> 30:56.604
There are a lot of people here.

30:57.146 --> 30:59.732
We didn't know.
Please, would you cut us some slack?

31:00.608 --> 31:02.151
[middle-aged Ae-sun] What's wrong?

31:02.235 --> 31:05.363
Why are you sighing?
How dare you sigh in front of people here!

31:06.155 --> 31:08.700
-Oh, my dear.
-Of course, first-timers don't know.

31:08.783 --> 31:10.994
You all give us attitude
and yell at people all day.

31:11.077 --> 31:12.412
Who do you think you are?

31:12.495 --> 31:14.914
You treat us like complete idiots
if we don't follow everything

31:14.998 --> 31:16.875
you already know,
like we're committing a crime.

31:16.958 --> 31:19.544
She's as smart as anyone.
Smarter than you. She is!

31:19.627 --> 31:21.754
-What happened? Mom, what?
-Geum-myeong, hi.

31:21.838 --> 31:24.299
Where have you been? We need you.

31:24.883 --> 31:27.719
Come with us when we visit the hospital.
Promise you will.

31:27.802 --> 31:29.470
You have to. Be here.

31:29.554 --> 31:30.597
[sighs]

31:32.056 --> 31:33.808
It's because Dad's sick.

31:34.475 --> 31:36.686
When you're sick, you get more frustrated.

31:37.353 --> 31:40.732
You get frustrated easily,
even if you only have a migraine.

31:42.108 --> 31:44.319
He's not mad at you, okay?

31:44.402 --> 31:45.445
[chuckles]

31:46.154 --> 31:49.866
You think Dad's always on my side,
no matter what?

31:50.617 --> 31:51.492
He's not.

31:51.993 --> 31:53.161
When you and I fight,

31:53.870 --> 31:55.788
Dad will always side with you first.

31:55.872 --> 31:56.956
[both chuckle]

31:57.749 --> 32:00.501
[Geum-myeong] If I'm his number one,
you're number zero.

32:01.377 --> 32:04.213
I think Dad sees you
as the precious One Ring.

32:04.297 --> 32:06.591
Anyone messes with you,
and they're dead meat.

32:09.761 --> 32:11.346
[gentle music playing]

32:17.310 --> 32:19.896
[Geum-myeong] All Dad saw was Mom.

32:22.565 --> 32:23.816
He saw Mom

32:24.817 --> 32:26.277
who would be sitting here

32:27.570 --> 32:29.030
all alone one day.

32:38.081 --> 32:38.915
Don't bother.

32:40.166 --> 32:42.293
Put me in a four-person room tomorrow.

32:42.377 --> 32:46.130
[sighs] I didn't get this room for you.
I did it for Mom's peace of mind.

32:47.006 --> 32:47.840
All right?

32:49.759 --> 32:53.388
I wouldn't have booked you
a VIP suite if you got sick. [laughs]

32:53.471 --> 32:55.431
I guess I lucked out with
you as my daughter.

32:55.515 --> 32:58.226
Then get well soon
and pay me back in other ways.

32:58.893 --> 33:00.812
You can watch Sae-bom for me

33:01.354 --> 33:03.106
and keep scaring my husband.

33:05.775 --> 33:07.860
He's being good to you, isn't he?

33:08.569 --> 33:09.904
The apple of his eye.

33:18.496 --> 33:20.331
So Chung-seop and I will come tomorrow.

33:20.415 --> 33:22.333
-We'll wash your hair.
-You're going?

33:23.126 --> 33:25.294
What? Like me to stay?

33:25.378 --> 33:27.880
You always tell me to go.
Why do you want me to stay?

33:28.631 --> 33:30.883
Sleep here. I'm all alone.

33:37.348 --> 33:40.268
They give the guardian
a pillow in the VIP suite.

33:40.351 --> 33:41.310
Wow, this is nice.

33:42.645 --> 33:44.397
How much is this place?

33:44.480 --> 33:46.441
You can go to Geum-myeong's to wash up.

33:47.316 --> 33:48.901
She'll be staying here tonight.

33:50.445 --> 33:51.654
[gentle music playing]

33:53.698 --> 33:56.659
[Geum-myeong] Crazy, because her mom
didn't have enough to bribe the teacher?

33:56.743 --> 33:59.495
That's how that kid's dad took away
Mom's class presidency?

33:59.579 --> 34:01.956
-That homeroom teacher was a bad man?
-A dick.

34:02.790 --> 34:03.624
A dick.

34:03.708 --> 34:05.877
[Geum-myeong laughs]

34:05.960 --> 34:07.420
[both laughing]

34:08.713 --> 34:12.050
So Mom head-butted that lady, really?

34:13.342 --> 34:15.470
-Yeah?
-Cracked that motel owner's nose…

34:15.553 --> 34:16.804
Pow! …with her head.

34:16.888 --> 34:18.681
[both laughing]

34:21.726 --> 34:23.102
So did you see Mom?

34:24.228 --> 34:26.147
Did you see her lying next to
Dong-myeong's grave?

34:27.440 --> 34:28.274
I did.

34:28.775 --> 34:29.609
[sobs]

34:29.692 --> 34:31.778
I followed her secretly 'cause I believed

34:32.445 --> 34:34.030
maybe she'd dive in the sea.

34:34.906 --> 34:36.407
How did she live through that?

34:36.949 --> 34:38.451
Your Mom was

34:39.452 --> 34:40.828
twenty-eight at the time.

34:42.747 --> 34:43.706
Twenty-eight.

34:46.626 --> 34:48.753
When I asked your mom to marry me,

34:48.836 --> 34:51.756
I promised her I'd either
pay for college on the mainland

34:53.049 --> 34:54.634
or help her become a poet.

34:56.636 --> 34:59.055
I vowed I'd do
one of those things for her,

35:00.389 --> 35:02.391
thinking I wouldn't even fulfill one.

35:03.518 --> 35:05.394
Mom's been writing these days.

35:06.395 --> 35:07.855
I love watching her write.

35:08.731 --> 35:11.234
She won a local writing competition once.

35:11.818 --> 35:14.112
In her high school class, she was first.

35:15.363 --> 35:17.740
That's how exceptional she is.

35:19.617 --> 35:22.078
Mom could've been
so much more than what she is.

35:26.791 --> 35:27.834
Be good to her.

35:27.917 --> 35:29.919
Promise, hmm?

35:32.046 --> 35:34.048
Dad, you're so annoying.

35:34.549 --> 35:37.176
You had me stay behind to tell me this?

35:39.137 --> 35:41.389
I'm sorry to burden you up to the end.

35:42.265 --> 35:44.392
I'm sorry I'm entrusting my bride to you.

35:45.476 --> 35:47.270
Where do you think you're going?

35:48.354 --> 35:49.897
You're not going anywhere.

35:49.981 --> 35:52.692
I don't want you to. I'm still a kid.

35:53.276 --> 35:54.777
You can't go till I'm grown.

35:55.403 --> 35:57.321
Why are you hell-bent on leaving us?

35:57.405 --> 35:58.489
[music fades]

35:59.115 --> 36:01.117
Geum-myeong, having you

36:02.326 --> 36:04.245
as my daughter was like

36:05.538 --> 36:07.039
catching a whale in a dinghy.

36:07.957 --> 36:10.668
You memorized the multiplication table
before anyone else.

36:10.751 --> 36:12.795
You went to Seoul National University.

36:13.838 --> 36:14.839
[chuckles]

36:15.882 --> 36:18.134
I had a full heart, yet I was sorry.

36:19.093 --> 36:20.720
I was sorry for you each day.

36:22.388 --> 36:24.515
I am truly sorry to you,

36:24.599 --> 36:25.850
but to your mom…

36:27.852 --> 36:29.353
my guilt is terrible.

36:32.273 --> 36:33.232
It keeps me awake.

36:34.317 --> 36:35.610
I can't sleep.

36:36.652 --> 36:38.863
Stay by Mom's side, then,
if it's that hard.

36:40.031 --> 36:41.866
Just stay with us a bit longer.

36:43.451 --> 36:44.285
Geum-myeong,

36:45.620 --> 36:47.246
you are my baby…

36:49.749 --> 36:51.500
and I'm sorry I'm leaving you.

36:52.960 --> 36:54.712
[sobs]

36:55.379 --> 36:56.339
Your mom

36:58.257 --> 37:00.092
means the world to me, okay?

37:02.386 --> 37:03.721
Don't treat her like

37:03.804 --> 37:05.598
she's being a pain.

37:06.390 --> 37:07.975
Don't get impatient with her,

37:09.602 --> 37:10.770
and be sweet to her.

37:13.231 --> 37:14.232
[sobs]

37:15.566 --> 37:16.442
Treat her well.

37:17.401 --> 37:18.819
[crying]

37:21.072 --> 37:22.406
How can I…

37:25.576 --> 37:28.621
How can I say goodbye to you? How?

37:35.461 --> 37:37.088
[wistful music playing]

37:39.006 --> 37:40.675
Oh, but Dad,

37:41.425 --> 37:42.802
I'm sorry, Dad.

37:42.885 --> 37:44.512
I'm sorry.

37:45.304 --> 37:48.057
Dad, sorry I get so annoyed. Mm?

37:49.850 --> 37:53.104
Sorry I'm always hanging up on you
and always rushed.

37:55.273 --> 37:59.986
But I was never actually
frustrated with you, you know?

38:01.612 --> 38:03.114
It was never that.

38:03.197 --> 38:04.615
Really, Dad.

38:09.412 --> 38:10.621
[middle-aged Gwan-sik] I know.

38:11.998 --> 38:13.165
Of course I know.

38:14.542 --> 38:16.502
I have the best daughter in the world.

38:20.047 --> 38:23.050
[Geum-myeong] I had a very loving father.

38:23.134 --> 38:25.886
So tell me,
is Dad coming to see me or not?

38:27.221 --> 38:28.431
[Geum-myeong] But my dad

38:29.056 --> 38:30.641
didn't have a loving daughter.

38:31.267 --> 38:33.644
"A big fish from a small pond."

38:34.770 --> 38:36.564
I really hate that saying.

38:37.398 --> 38:40.693
What good is it that you're a fish
that made it out of the pond?

38:40.776 --> 38:42.403
The pillar, the older sibling.

38:42.486 --> 38:44.780
-God, I'm sick of it all!
-Yang Geum-myeong!

38:45.781 --> 38:48.993
[Geum-myeong] His loving request
for me to be sweet to my mom

38:50.036 --> 38:52.413
still stings in my heart.

38:52.496 --> 38:55.291
You want me to live like you?
Is that what you want?

38:55.374 --> 38:57.460
Yes, because I didn't wanna live like you.

38:57.960 --> 39:00.671
I just couldn't live like
you and mom did. I hated it, you know?

39:00.755 --> 39:04.342
You smelled like cooling patches
every day. What have you done for me?

39:05.009 --> 39:06.427
[Geum-myeong] We treated him

39:07.845 --> 39:09.722
as if we'd have him forever.

39:11.390 --> 39:13.601
[Hyeon-suk] Is it okay for him
to be at home?

39:14.352 --> 39:15.519
That's what he'd like.

39:16.270 --> 39:18.773
He says he wants
to live at home for a while.

39:19.648 --> 39:21.025
He wants to see the sea.

39:22.068 --> 39:25.321
It might be better for him
if he stays home with us.

39:25.404 --> 39:26.864
[middle-aged Ae-sun] Careful.

39:39.585 --> 39:43.506
Dad, sit on this stationary bike
so your back feels better, okay?

39:44.173 --> 39:47.009
Or you can sit here
and just listen to Kim Kwang-seok.

39:47.802 --> 39:50.763
I also scoured the Internet
and got this vinyl.

39:51.555 --> 39:52.473
Here's a guitar.

39:53.599 --> 39:54.683
[sobs]

39:56.519 --> 39:57.353
Oh, Dad,

39:58.020 --> 39:59.021
how…

39:59.605 --> 40:00.439
how did you…

40:02.358 --> 40:03.734
how did you become so thin?

40:05.319 --> 40:06.362
Dad.

40:06.445 --> 40:07.571
[emotional music playing]

40:07.655 --> 40:08.781
Oh, Dad.

40:08.864 --> 40:10.241
Why, Dad?

40:10.324 --> 40:13.994
Hey, you're a dad yourself now.
You gotta be strong, son.

40:15.913 --> 40:17.415
Dad, why are you doing this?

40:19.333 --> 40:21.293
There's so much I wanted to do for you.

40:22.378 --> 40:24.088
I said I'd buy you a Mercedes.

40:24.672 --> 40:26.340
I wanted to get you another boat.

40:27.633 --> 40:28.843
I've been in one before.

40:29.427 --> 40:30.845
I don't need another one.

40:33.806 --> 40:35.141
You've been a good son.

40:38.227 --> 40:39.186
I already know.

40:39.854 --> 40:41.814
I always knew, but I…

40:43.315 --> 40:44.150
I…

40:45.985 --> 40:49.572
[grandma] Your brother died
three days after your birthday.

40:50.072 --> 40:51.907
They can't celebrate it, understand?

40:51.991 --> 40:54.034
That's not fair.

40:54.618 --> 40:57.371
I don't wanna!

40:58.664 --> 40:59.999
[young Eun-myeong crying]

41:02.209 --> 41:03.794
Eun-myeong, come here.

41:12.511 --> 41:14.180
[Gwan-sik] Eun-myeong, choose one.

41:14.263 --> 41:18.058
We can do some rice cakes at the house
or have sweet and sour pork here.

41:18.142 --> 41:19.768
Can't do both. You can pick only one.

41:21.145 --> 41:22.771
What are you trying?

41:25.441 --> 41:28.027
I'll buy you those secretly then,
or should I not?

41:30.279 --> 41:32.948
Then you'll keep this our secret, yeah?

41:34.241 --> 41:35.910
You're going to tell your sister,

41:36.702 --> 41:37.536
aren't you?

41:38.037 --> 41:39.038
Tattletale.

41:39.872 --> 41:43.709
Sometimes you like me better
than Geum-myeong, I think, Dad.

41:43.792 --> 41:44.877
[laughs]

41:46.962 --> 41:47.796
Have some pork.

41:47.880 --> 41:49.465
[Eun-myeong] You bought that just for me.

41:50.132 --> 41:51.509
And you did it secretly.

41:52.885 --> 41:54.220
I know all that.

41:57.097 --> 41:59.183
See, I do remember the good stuff.

41:59.266 --> 42:00.726
You tattletale.

42:01.602 --> 42:03.020
You're turning me in now?

42:04.730 --> 42:06.065
I'm an asshole.

42:08.734 --> 42:10.986
Oh, now you're bombarding me with insults.

42:11.904 --> 42:13.781
[Eun-myeong crying]

42:16.825 --> 42:18.786
[middle-aged Ae-sun]
The aunties harvested these.

42:19.286 --> 42:21.914
That damn sea.
It must know I'm angry you're sick.

42:21.997 --> 42:24.124
They were apparently so easy to harvest.

42:25.918 --> 42:27.586
[Geum-myeong] The sea provided endlessly,

42:27.670 --> 42:30.297
no matter how much
we harvested in our lives.

42:31.298 --> 42:33.217
[middle-aged Gwan-sik]
Mom, your son's here.

42:33.801 --> 42:35.052
Wash up quickly.

42:35.928 --> 42:37.263
[Gye-ok] Wash up and eat.

42:40.599 --> 42:41.559
[Geum-myeong] To us,

42:42.351 --> 42:43.852
Dad was the sea.

42:46.730 --> 42:49.191
We all relied on him to live.

42:49.692 --> 42:51.443
[crying]

42:54.572 --> 42:56.532
[man on TV] One day,
this petite person brought me

42:56.615 --> 42:59.994
a can of Cherry Coke and offered me
a contract to work with her.

43:00.619 --> 43:02.371
She told me with conviction that…

43:02.454 --> 43:04.707
You see, courses on tape are the future.

43:05.332 --> 43:08.043
[man on TV] Honestly,
I found it ridiculous at first,

43:08.544 --> 43:10.254
but as soon as
I heard of the company name,

43:10.754 --> 43:13.132
I remember thinking I'd give it a chance.

43:13.882 --> 43:16.969
The next speaker
that I will bring to the stage

43:17.052 --> 43:19.680
is someone who is going
to change the industry.

43:20.472 --> 43:23.642
Please welcome the CEO of Ever Study,
Yang Geum-myeong.

43:23.726 --> 43:25.436
[audience cheering]

43:25.519 --> 43:27.438
TODAY'S NOTABLE LECTURER
YANG GEUM-MYEONG, CEO

43:27.521 --> 43:31.317
Ooh! It's Geum-myeong. It's Geum-myeong.

43:32.234 --> 43:33.986
[Geum-myeong] We had to repay our debt.

43:34.570 --> 43:38.282
We shone the pathway
for a farewell with a fanfare.

43:38.365 --> 43:40.826
Hello, my name is Yang Geum-myeong.

43:41.785 --> 43:43.329
I studied in Japan,

43:43.912 --> 43:47.458
and I used to listen to lectures
over and over again.

43:48.375 --> 43:50.294
Because I couldn't speak the language,

43:50.794 --> 43:52.713
this was all I had to rely on.

43:54.298 --> 43:55.758
I thought to myself,

43:55.841 --> 43:59.261
"Wouldn't it be great if I could
keep the teacher in my pocket?"

43:59.345 --> 44:02.765
One day, I was in my hometown,
staring at the bookcase.

44:02.848 --> 44:03.849
And it

44:04.600 --> 44:05.893
hit like a truck.

44:07.770 --> 44:10.731
I, uh, saw an old workbook

44:12.316 --> 44:14.568
for my mom's college entrance exam.

44:15.819 --> 44:17.780
[middle-aged Ae-sun]
Is she talking about me?

44:18.405 --> 44:22.076
My mother was exceptional through
every part of her life.

44:22.159 --> 44:24.662
She was smart and diligent,

44:24.745 --> 44:27.039
and she really wanted to pursue

44:27.748 --> 44:29.500
a higher education.

44:30.084 --> 44:33.962
Had my mom been given access
to classes in the palm of her hand,

44:34.046 --> 44:36.215
she could have studied
to her heart's content.

44:36.882 --> 44:38.676
My mom would've thrived.

44:39.343 --> 44:43.430
Even if she never lived in Daechi-dong
and didn't have expensive tutors,

44:43.514 --> 44:47.559
the bookworm on Jeju Island
should've been able to study.

44:50.104 --> 44:52.606
I think anyone who wants to study

44:53.857 --> 44:55.693
should be able to do so,

44:55.776 --> 44:58.737
whoever, whenever, wherever.

44:59.321 --> 45:00.406
Ever Study.

45:01.699 --> 45:03.075
It all began

45:03.951 --> 45:05.452
as my mother's dream.

45:05.953 --> 45:07.287
Her childhood dream.

45:07.371 --> 45:08.872
[audience cheering]

45:09.665 --> 45:10.666
Aw!

45:13.210 --> 45:14.253
I can't believe it.

45:15.170 --> 45:17.506
I can't believe her. [chuckles]

45:17.589 --> 45:19.800
She's quite the saleswoman there.

45:19.883 --> 45:21.969
[sobs]

45:22.511 --> 45:23.554
[Geum-myeong] And then,

45:23.637 --> 45:27.683
high-speed Internet user numbers
surpassed ten million people.

45:27.766 --> 45:30.227
Tech made video conferencing a reality.

45:30.310 --> 45:33.439
Divided families in North and South Korea
were able to speak again.

45:34.022 --> 45:36.734
I knew the age of online classes
would come one day.

45:36.817 --> 45:40.279
So I seized the possibility
with the persevering spirit

45:40.362 --> 45:41.613
that I inherited from my father.

45:41.697 --> 45:43.198
She mentioned me too. She did.

45:43.282 --> 45:44.575
[wistful music playing]

45:44.658 --> 45:46.160
[Geum-myeong] There were things

45:46.660 --> 45:48.871
that I wanted to show my dad.

45:49.455 --> 45:51.874
[reporter] Today, the Haenyeo Museum
has opened to celebrate

45:51.957 --> 45:54.084
the pride and the history
of Jeju's haenyeo.

45:54.168 --> 45:55.711
[man] Right here. Perfect. That's great.

45:55.794 --> 45:58.547
[woman 5] By opening this museum
that shows

45:59.131 --> 46:02.509
the pride and the history
of the Jeju haenyeo,

46:02.593 --> 46:07.097
we can show everyone
the world of the haenyeo.

46:07.181 --> 46:10.517
To be included in the list
of World Heritage sites,

46:10.601 --> 46:12.728
we want to show that we have

46:14.062 --> 46:15.522
a living job.

46:15.606 --> 46:16.982
And we are still alive.

46:17.065 --> 46:19.985
Our culture's alive, just as we are.

46:20.068 --> 46:22.696
We want to do our best to revive.

46:22.780 --> 46:24.698
-Preserve, inherit.
-[Eun-myeong] Are you serious?

46:24.782 --> 46:26.742
How can you do this to your dad?

46:26.825 --> 46:29.787
You took cash from my wallet
for an A-reum headband. Really?

46:29.870 --> 46:32.998
It's not A-reum, you know.
It's Jeong A-ram.

46:33.791 --> 46:36.543
Honey, did you do these highlights
on our son?

46:37.252 --> 46:39.630
-Say, "Ah."
-[Eun-myeong] Look at this boy.

46:40.756 --> 46:43.967
You'll go to school with these highlights?
You have a crush on that girl, right?

46:44.051 --> 46:47.679
-Mom and Dad already know.
-Your dad can do it all. Mr. MacGyver.

46:49.056 --> 46:51.183
[Eun-myeong] Dad,
why do you keep laughing?

46:51.683 --> 46:54.019
It's like you laugh
every time I yell at Je-il.

46:54.102 --> 46:56.897
[laughs] What goes around
comes around, huh?

46:57.648 --> 46:59.900
You always reap what you sow.
Revenge is sweet.

47:05.614 --> 47:06.740
What?

47:08.826 --> 47:10.202
Unbelievable.

47:12.329 --> 47:13.372
Babe.

47:14.289 --> 47:16.583
[middle-aged Gwan-sik]
What? What is it now?

47:16.667 --> 47:18.418
Oh, it's not real.

47:19.127 --> 47:21.088
Why can't we have
a moment's peace in this house?

47:21.964 --> 47:23.090
What is it now?

47:24.716 --> 47:26.301
You kept your word.

47:26.927 --> 47:30.138
The promise. You kept one out of three.

47:38.480 --> 47:39.982
[sentimental music playing]

47:42.442 --> 47:45.279
[middle-aged Ae-sun] "To the one
who will be leaving me behind."

47:45.362 --> 47:48.365
"Oh Ae-sun of Dodong-dong Jeju."

47:49.324 --> 47:53.036
"When I was young, I thought I had to
hold your hand to feel warmth."

47:53.912 --> 47:55.622
"Now I know you're with me

47:55.706 --> 47:57.457
even when you're not around."

47:59.001 --> 48:01.003
"Now I have a warm floor."

48:01.879 --> 48:04.798
"Just the thought of you warms my heart."

48:06.550 --> 48:09.595
"I will go on knowing
that the moon is in the sky

48:09.678 --> 48:11.179
even during the day."

48:11.972 --> 48:14.266
"So when it's time for you to go,

48:14.349 --> 48:15.934
spread your wings and fly."

48:16.518 --> 48:18.687
"After 50 years, you can fly free."

48:18.770 --> 48:20.647
"You can let me go now."

48:20.731 --> 48:22.524
"My precious love,

48:22.608 --> 48:24.568
I'm eternally thankful to you."

48:25.152 --> 48:26.737
"You showed me what to do

48:27.237 --> 48:29.281
when life gives you tangerines."

48:37.164 --> 48:39.666
You've been crying a lot more lately.

48:44.212 --> 48:45.464
[sighs, sniffles]

48:47.674 --> 48:50.928
You see? You kept one promise, after all.

48:52.554 --> 48:55.641
Now I'm a published poet, you see?

48:56.642 --> 49:00.062
Yeah, but if you weren't with me,
it wouldn't have taken so long.

49:00.646 --> 49:02.898
I couldn't be doing it without you.

49:02.981 --> 49:05.233
I couldn't write poems like this.

49:06.735 --> 49:07.819
Ah, well.

49:08.320 --> 49:09.571
Damn it, Ae-sun.

49:09.655 --> 49:11.448
-[laughs]
-Damn it, Ae-sun.

49:11.531 --> 49:12.783
[both laugh]

49:14.576 --> 49:15.410
You thrilled?

49:17.412 --> 49:18.747
Oh yes.

49:20.207 --> 49:21.041
This is

49:21.875 --> 49:23.043
everything.

49:23.126 --> 49:24.711
[both laughing]

49:27.130 --> 49:28.465
[kissing]

49:29.466 --> 49:31.510
Grandma and Grandpa are kissing.

49:32.594 --> 49:33.595
Oh. Piggyback?

49:33.679 --> 49:35.472
-[middle-aged Gwan-sik] Get on.
-I'm heavy.

49:35.555 --> 49:37.891
-Hey, my kids are watching. Be careful.
-You sure? Careful.

49:37.975 --> 49:40.102
If you and Mom keep doing that,
they'll think romance is

49:40.185 --> 49:41.561
the best thing in the world.

49:42.229 --> 49:46.108
Hey, buy a hundred of Mom's books
and give them to the fishing village.

49:46.191 --> 49:47.109
You have to.

49:47.192 --> 49:49.194
[laughter]

49:52.197 --> 49:54.282
[Geum-myeong] She wanted time
to stop that day.

49:54.783 --> 49:56.910
She wanted the bonus track to never end.

49:58.245 --> 50:01.331
Mom wanted that night to last forever.

50:06.086 --> 50:07.337
[music fades]

50:07.421 --> 50:08.672
[middle-aged Ae-sun] Honey.

50:10.132 --> 50:11.883
Can we keep living like this?

50:13.635 --> 50:15.262
I'd love it if we could get

50:15.846 --> 50:17.806
five more years together.

50:22.227 --> 50:23.103
Or

50:24.730 --> 50:26.314
at least one more year.

50:27.524 --> 50:29.985
To experience seasons, okay?

50:30.485 --> 50:32.738
I thought I may not be able to fulfill

50:33.780 --> 50:35.282
even one of the three.

50:36.033 --> 50:37.909
Now that you're writing poems again,

50:39.369 --> 50:40.871
I feel much better.

50:41.872 --> 50:42.873
Much better.

50:44.207 --> 50:45.876
In my next life,

50:47.627 --> 50:50.630
I'll do five, ten promises.

50:53.258 --> 50:54.509
Wanna be there with me?

51:01.683 --> 51:02.893
You believe

51:04.561 --> 51:05.896
we'll meet there?

51:07.272 --> 51:08.106
Why?

51:09.316 --> 51:10.776
Don't wanna be there with me?

51:16.406 --> 51:18.408
Such blessings

51:18.492 --> 51:19.910
don't come easily.

51:22.162 --> 51:24.873
Others deserve a chance
to live the good life.

51:27.876 --> 51:30.587
It's my fault you suffered
your entire life.

51:32.547 --> 51:34.132
I was never lonely

51:35.675 --> 51:37.427
because of you, dear.

51:39.805 --> 51:40.806
Not a day.

51:43.767 --> 51:45.769
It was a wonderful life.

51:48.063 --> 51:48.897
Ae-sun.

51:49.815 --> 51:50.649
Huh?

51:51.233 --> 51:52.984
I have one thing to ask of you.

51:56.655 --> 51:57.823
Don't weep a lot…

51:59.908 --> 52:01.034
when the time's near.

52:03.495 --> 52:05.122
It's always hard for me

52:06.623 --> 52:08.041
when you weep like that.

52:11.169 --> 52:13.004
I'd never be able to fly away.

52:15.674 --> 52:17.008
What I wanna see…

52:19.094 --> 52:21.638
What I really wanna see
in my last minutes…

52:24.850 --> 52:26.309
is your smile.

52:28.770 --> 52:30.188
Life was full of joy

52:31.565 --> 52:33.733
'cause of your beautiful laughter, Ae-sun.

52:44.119 --> 52:45.579
-[sobs]
-Hey.

52:46.121 --> 52:48.415
You can't even do that?

52:51.084 --> 52:52.544
Pat me on the back.

53:06.600 --> 53:08.185
♪ Sleep ♪

53:08.685 --> 53:09.769
♪ Sleep ♪

53:12.689 --> 53:14.941
♪ Sweet child ♪

53:16.902 --> 53:17.986
♪ Sleep ♪

53:18.570 --> 53:22.574
♪ Sleep, sweet child, rest ♪

53:22.657 --> 53:23.950
[wistful piano music playing]

53:24.034 --> 53:25.577
[crying]

53:25.660 --> 53:31.166
♪ My baby is fast asleep ♪

53:33.376 --> 53:35.837
♪ Sleep now ♪

53:35.921 --> 53:37.797
♪ Sleep now ♪

53:40.217 --> 53:43.053
♪ Little black dog ♪

53:43.136 --> 53:45.388
♪ As you go ♪

53:46.640 --> 53:49.768
♪ Little black dog ♪

53:50.268 --> 53:52.604
♪ As you come ♪

53:53.730 --> 53:58.485
♪ Help my baby sleep well ♪

54:00.237 --> 54:05.784
♪ I'll help your babies sleep well ♪

54:06.785 --> 54:09.120
[Geum-myeong] Mom always said
she had hard days,

54:09.788 --> 54:11.790
but she never had lonely ones.

54:11.873 --> 54:14.793
In hindsight, my mother lived in paradise.

54:14.876 --> 54:16.962
Oh, wow. Wow, that's terrific.

54:17.837 --> 54:20.757
[Geum-myeong] My dad spent all his life
patting us on our backs.

54:22.342 --> 54:26.179
He did his best for us
with all the strength he had in him.

54:26.263 --> 54:28.640
[Chung-seop] Sweetie,
you'll have an accident.

54:28.723 --> 54:30.850
Why don't you pull over somewhere?
I'll be right there.

54:30.934 --> 54:32.560
It's okay.

54:33.436 --> 54:35.438
There aren't any cars.

54:35.522 --> 54:37.857
-There aren't any cars on the road.
-No cars?

54:38.942 --> 54:42.362
[Geum-myeong] Dad, don't go
before I see you. Not before then.

54:42.862 --> 54:45.448
[Geum-myeong] Heaven showed us mercy
one last time.

54:45.532 --> 54:47.867
-So that we could escort him there.
-I'm here.

54:47.951 --> 54:50.036
I'm here, Dad. Dad, I'm right here.

54:50.537 --> 54:51.371
Dad.

54:51.871 --> 54:54.749
Dad, I'm right here. Dad, don't be scared.

54:54.833 --> 54:56.084
Don't be scared, okay?

54:56.584 --> 54:58.962
I'm sorry, Dad.

54:59.838 --> 55:02.299
Dad, Dad, Dad, I love you.

55:02.382 --> 55:05.135
-I'm sorry, Dad. Dad.
-[Geum-myeong] Dad, I love you.

55:06.386 --> 55:08.013
-Dad.
-[middle-aged Ae-sun] Honey.

55:08.096 --> 55:09.556
[Eun-myeong] Dad, I'm sorry.

55:10.557 --> 55:14.602
[Geum-myeong] The last look
that Dad got to see on our faces

55:15.186 --> 55:16.521
was a sadness

55:17.272 --> 55:19.024
he'd never seen before.

55:23.820 --> 55:25.822
[emotional pop ballad playing]

55:31.828 --> 55:33.371
[middle-aged Ae-sun sniffles]

55:35.081 --> 55:36.499
[sobs]

55:52.015 --> 55:54.351
[middle-aged Ae-sun]
You should've been easier on yourself.

55:54.851 --> 55:56.478
You've grown old so fast.

55:58.688 --> 56:00.565
[middle-aged Gwan-sik]
But you're still the same.

56:00.648 --> 56:02.108
[crying]

56:04.194 --> 56:05.820
[middle-aged Ae-sun] I've grown old too.

56:08.239 --> 56:09.532
[middle-aged Gwan-sik] No.

56:10.116 --> 56:11.284
You're the same.

56:13.203 --> 56:15.288
In my eyes, you've never changed

56:16.373 --> 56:17.665
in 50 years.

56:30.553 --> 56:34.057
[Geum-myeong] There was a girl
in a boy's life.

56:36.768 --> 56:38.603
He spent all his life

56:39.145 --> 56:41.356
keeping the girl's world safe.

56:43.900 --> 56:44.859
[Ae-sun] Thank you,

56:45.652 --> 56:46.486
honey.

56:48.238 --> 56:50.573
You lived a good life.

56:51.533 --> 56:53.410
We had a good life.

56:57.539 --> 56:58.706
[Gwan-sik] Was it good?

57:01.751 --> 57:05.088
[middle-aged Gwan-sik]
Was your life with me any good?

57:07.257 --> 57:09.342
[middle-aged Ae-sun]
I didn't need anything else.

57:13.513 --> 57:14.889
[middle-aged Ae-sun sobs]

57:18.101 --> 57:20.937
It was so good
that I didn't need anything more.

57:22.397 --> 57:23.982
[emotional music playing]

57:24.065 --> 57:28.611
[Geum-myeong] As he looked into the eyes
of the one who was ingrained in his soul…

57:34.659 --> 57:37.620
Dad slept in for the first time.

57:42.167 --> 57:44.586
[monitor beeping]

57:49.090 --> 57:50.633
[Geum-myeong] He left many gifts behind.

57:54.429 --> 57:56.973
[Gye-ok] Your dad wanted you to have this.

57:58.391 --> 57:59.601
[music fades]

58:01.936 --> 58:03.771
[Geum-myeong] Through all these years,

58:04.397 --> 58:05.732
Dad never spent

58:06.357 --> 58:08.943
any of the money I sent him and Mom.

58:09.027 --> 58:11.154
[Gye-ok] He never withdrew
from this account,

58:11.237 --> 58:13.531
but he would always
check up on it here and there.

58:14.032 --> 58:15.408
He said it made him so happy

58:15.492 --> 58:17.785
that his daughter
could manage sending that much money.

58:19.537 --> 58:21.498
Oh, why didn't he use it?

58:21.581 --> 58:23.082
[Gye-ok] When you sent 100,000 won,

58:23.166 --> 58:26.085
he said he'd feel a joy
worth a million won.

58:29.047 --> 58:30.256
But all he had

58:31.174 --> 58:32.967
was one closet to his name.

58:35.303 --> 58:37.889
God, Dad, why are you so annoying?

58:37.972 --> 58:41.100
[Geum-myeong] Dad's unrequited love
was now over,

58:41.184 --> 58:42.936
but mine had just begun.

58:43.019 --> 58:44.020
[sighs]

58:49.526 --> 58:51.945
[Sang-gil] Your father wanted you
to have a Mercedes.

58:52.779 --> 58:55.949
He wanted you to live a great life.

58:57.867 --> 59:00.245
Hmm. What's the odometer read?

59:02.872 --> 59:03.873
That's crazy.

59:04.791 --> 59:07.627
You are so similar to my daughter.

59:23.184 --> 59:24.644
[middle-aged Gwan-sik]
You wear those hairpins every day,

59:24.727 --> 59:26.563
and I keep looking for them all the time.

59:26.646 --> 59:29.607
Why do I bother buying them for you?
You keep losing them anyway.

59:57.594 --> 01:00:01.389
[Geum-myeong] There was a 50-year love
on Mom's Treasure Island.

01:00:18.281 --> 01:00:19.574
It was a love

01:00:20.283 --> 01:00:21.826
that would never die.

01:00:29.083 --> 01:00:30.126
[sighs]

01:00:30.209 --> 01:00:31.544
[emotional music playing]

01:00:34.797 --> 01:00:36.591
What am I supposed to do?

01:00:40.887 --> 01:00:42.347
How do I go on?

01:01:05.620 --> 01:01:07.538
[middle-aged Gwan-sik]
Stop making rolled omelets.

01:01:09.999 --> 01:01:12.460
You never could eat sujebi
after Dong-myeong left us.

01:01:13.503 --> 01:01:15.672
You might cry
seeing rolled omelets when I'm gone.

01:01:35.858 --> 01:01:38.820
If the kids want you
to live with them, go.

01:01:38.903 --> 01:01:40.279
That's what I'd want.

01:01:41.698 --> 01:01:43.282
If you have to live without me,

01:01:43.950 --> 01:01:45.284
don't do it alone.

01:01:50.373 --> 01:01:51.958
[kettle whistling]

01:02:19.110 --> 01:02:20.027
Oh.

01:02:21.237 --> 01:02:23.489
When did he take these down?

01:02:32.290 --> 01:02:33.332
[thunder rumbling]

01:02:40.423 --> 01:02:41.674
Boy, my love

01:02:42.759 --> 01:02:44.302
was so busy.

01:02:45.970 --> 01:02:47.472
[Geum-myeong] Just as we know

01:02:47.555 --> 01:02:50.600
the moon is somewhere in the sky
during the day,

01:02:50.683 --> 01:02:53.227
Mom knew Dad was always there.

01:02:55.521 --> 01:02:57.523
[wistful music playing]

01:03:03.738 --> 01:03:08.367
SEEING A LOVED ONE RETURN EACH DAY
THROUGH THE DOOR THEY LEFT IN THE MORNING.

01:03:08.451 --> 01:03:12.663
IT WAS LIKE A MIRACLE EVERY DAY.

01:03:22.673 --> 01:03:24.133
I've written a lot.

01:03:26.010 --> 01:03:27.595
So many poems.

01:03:33.476 --> 01:03:35.311
Let's have another go.

01:03:39.106 --> 01:03:41.108
OH AE-SUN

01:03:44.362 --> 01:03:46.906
[Geum-myeong] Just as white snow
covers the earth,

01:03:47.615 --> 01:03:50.243
time covers all the noise and sorrow.

01:03:53.287 --> 01:03:55.540
Winter had finally arrived.

01:03:58.376 --> 01:03:59.794
[middle-aged Ae-sun] I'll be back.

01:04:00.962 --> 01:04:02.338
I'll see you again.

01:04:03.589 --> 01:04:04.715
[chuckles]

01:04:12.306 --> 01:04:13.516
You see, sir,

01:04:14.100 --> 01:04:17.603
that's just where my husband is,
right there.

01:04:28.155 --> 01:04:29.073
Have a look.

01:04:29.866 --> 01:04:31.742
I did write the entire thing.

01:04:32.326 --> 01:04:33.452
I finished.

01:04:35.496 --> 01:04:36.414
[chuckles]

01:04:38.583 --> 01:04:41.210
[Geum-myeong] I believe their story
should never be forgotten.

01:04:41.294 --> 01:04:44.463
I'm sending you the 70-year story
of my parents' lives.

01:04:44.547 --> 01:04:48.926
From Yang Geum-myeong, the eldest child of
Yang Gwan-sik and Oh Ae-sun.

01:04:49.427 --> 01:04:52.054
♪ …though they're here to stay ♪

01:04:52.138 --> 01:04:54.599
♪ Oh, I believe ♪

01:04:54.682 --> 01:04:57.393
♪ In yesterday ♪

01:04:57.476 --> 01:04:59.604
♪ Suddenly… ♪

01:05:00.438 --> 01:05:05.651
You know, the things that you've
most wanted to say inside.

01:05:05.735 --> 01:05:09.405
♪ There's a shadow hanging over me ♪

01:05:09.488 --> 01:05:14.577
♪ Oh, yesterday came suddenly ♪

01:05:14.660 --> 01:05:19.165
♪ Why she had to go ♪

01:05:19.248 --> 01:05:21.751
♪ I don't know, she wouldn't say… ♪

01:05:21.834 --> 01:05:25.421
Excuse me, Teacher Ae-sun.
Can you color this for me?

01:05:26.005 --> 01:05:30.134
[middle-aged Ae-sun] Jeez, why do you keep
asking me to do things for you?

01:05:30.217 --> 01:05:32.428
It's time you start doing it alone.

01:05:33.804 --> 01:05:36.307
Learn to draw by yourself

01:05:36.933 --> 01:05:38.893
and speak to yourself.

01:05:38.976 --> 01:05:40.728
Play some cards alone

01:05:41.395 --> 01:05:43.439
so you don't become sick.

01:05:44.315 --> 01:05:46.400
You get sick when you're lonely.

01:05:47.234 --> 01:05:50.529
Jeez, why do you keep giving me yours?

01:05:50.613 --> 01:05:51.614
I went

01:05:52.490 --> 01:05:56.410
to your restaurant
with my daughter and her husband.

01:05:56.494 --> 01:05:58.496
I ordered the food myself.

01:05:58.579 --> 01:05:59.956
It's 'cause of you.

01:06:00.790 --> 01:06:03.751
"Jeong Gong-rye, the Illiterate Woman."

01:06:03.834 --> 01:06:06.087
I've been embarrassed all my life

01:06:06.170 --> 01:06:09.215
that I didn't go to school
because I was a haenyeo.

01:06:09.715 --> 01:06:13.678
When anyone asked me
to order something from the menu,

01:06:13.761 --> 01:06:16.097
my heart sank every time.

01:06:16.180 --> 01:06:20.977
But yesterday, I ordered
what I wanted to eat all by myself.

01:06:21.519 --> 01:06:23.396
I ordered a big plate of sushi.

01:06:23.479 --> 01:06:26.524
It was the best thing that I ever had.

01:06:26.607 --> 01:06:27.984
[woman] Teacher Ae-sun,

01:06:29.318 --> 01:06:30.236
have a little.

01:06:30.319 --> 01:06:33.197
-Here.
-Oh, why do you keep giving me things?

01:06:33.781 --> 01:06:36.033
You're pretty. You are.

01:06:36.117 --> 01:06:38.202
Do I remind you of your daughter again?

01:06:39.453 --> 01:06:44.542
Oh, how I would have loved it to see
my daughter work at a desk just like you.

01:06:44.625 --> 01:06:46.085
It would be great, my dear,

01:06:46.168 --> 01:06:49.255
if you could earn a living at a desk
like your teacher in elementary school.

01:06:49.338 --> 01:06:50.464
[chuckles]

01:06:53.384 --> 01:06:54.427
Mm.

01:06:55.928 --> 01:06:59.265
[middle-aged Ae-sun] I wish my mother
was here to peel these tangerines.

01:06:59.348 --> 01:07:02.059
I wanna eat a big plate of sushi too.

01:07:03.060 --> 01:07:06.564
The word I wanted to say
again the most in my life…

01:07:07.982 --> 01:07:08.941
Mom.

01:07:11.235 --> 01:07:12.319
Mom.

01:07:13.320 --> 01:07:14.697
Mom!

01:07:16.282 --> 01:07:18.451
Mom!

01:07:19.618 --> 01:07:20.786
[sighs]

01:07:21.412 --> 01:07:23.873
Other people live to 90 and 100 years.

01:07:24.457 --> 01:07:26.250
Why were you so eager to go?

01:07:26.959 --> 01:07:29.503
Were you reborn into a better life?

01:07:30.463 --> 01:07:32.673
I hope that you get to work at a desk

01:07:32.757 --> 01:07:35.176
like you wanted, to boss people around.

01:07:35.259 --> 01:07:36.802
[phone ringing]

01:07:42.099 --> 01:07:43.100
MY DAUGHTER

01:07:45.644 --> 01:07:46.562
Hi.

01:07:46.645 --> 01:07:48.147
How am I?

01:07:49.607 --> 01:07:52.943
Well, same ol', same ol', you know.

01:07:54.278 --> 01:07:55.112
What?

01:07:56.947 --> 01:07:58.032
Oh, but why now?

01:07:58.115 --> 01:08:00.117
[feel-good music playing]

01:08:01.035 --> 01:08:03.079
[middle-aged Ae-sun] You said
you couldn't come this month.

01:08:03.162 --> 01:08:07.750
Jeez, I shouldn't have given
the sour kimchi to your aunt.

01:08:08.250 --> 01:08:11.462
Hey, Mom, stop it and just come sit down.

01:08:11.545 --> 01:08:14.548
-Sit down now.
-[middle-aged Ae-sun] You like it sour?

01:08:14.632 --> 01:08:17.093
Eun-myeong likes to have it fresh.

01:08:17.176 --> 01:08:19.386
I always have to have those separate.

01:08:20.346 --> 01:08:21.305
Oh my God.

01:08:21.806 --> 01:08:24.475
[Geum-myeong] Mom had been lonely
up until the day before,

01:08:24.558 --> 01:08:27.061
but she turned into that young girl again.

01:08:28.646 --> 01:08:31.524
Their boat was full once again.

01:08:33.192 --> 01:08:34.360
[singing]

01:08:35.444 --> 01:08:37.863
Mother, look, Lim Young-woong is on.

01:08:41.450 --> 01:08:42.576
Oh my.

01:08:47.206 --> 01:08:50.292
[Eun-myeong] Mom, why are you
so into Lim Young-woong?

01:08:51.752 --> 01:08:54.046
[middle-aged Ae-sun]
Your father loved Kim Kwang-seok.

01:08:54.630 --> 01:08:57.174
He learned guitar
so he could play this song.

01:08:57.675 --> 01:09:00.636
But he never sang it for me because

01:09:01.387 --> 01:09:02.555
he thought he'd cry.

01:09:03.514 --> 01:09:05.766
But now Young-woong is singing it.

01:09:07.977 --> 01:09:08.853
Aw!

01:09:09.353 --> 01:09:10.563
It's a beautiful song.

01:09:12.356 --> 01:09:15.359
[Geum-myeong] Mom,
how do you stay young like that?

01:09:16.318 --> 01:09:18.988
[Geum-myeong] She was still
like a fragile flower petal.

01:09:19.071 --> 01:09:20.781
HAENYEO MUSEUM

01:09:20.865 --> 01:09:24.827
UNESCO INTANGIBLE CULTURAL HERITAGE
HAENYEO PERFORMANCE - LET'S GO TOGETHER

01:09:25.828 --> 01:09:27.872
And she still had dreams.

01:09:29.456 --> 01:09:31.333
Let's go to the hospital together.

01:09:31.917 --> 01:09:33.752
You don't need favors from our kids.

01:09:34.253 --> 01:09:36.505
If you get sick, I'll take care of you.

01:09:37.631 --> 01:09:40.384
Better that you take
a bit more care for yourself.

01:09:40.968 --> 01:09:42.970
What are you doing about that belly?

01:09:43.679 --> 01:09:45.389
The kids are already judging you.

01:09:45.472 --> 01:09:48.350
And you should dye your hair. God.

01:09:50.227 --> 01:09:51.270
Dye it?

01:09:52.479 --> 01:09:53.981
-Will you help me?
-[sighs]

01:09:56.358 --> 01:09:59.945
So is there an age limit to first love?

01:10:00.029 --> 01:10:02.239
God, stop talking, please.

01:10:03.032 --> 01:10:06.118
-If there isn't, I was wondering if we…
-All right, let me out. Let me out.

01:10:06.202 --> 01:10:08.370
But the car is moving.
How can you ask that?

01:10:08.871 --> 01:10:10.664
Keep driving. Eyes on the road.

01:10:11.999 --> 01:10:14.251
[Sang-gil] I'm not
your chauffeur now, am I?

01:10:15.169 --> 01:10:17.421
[Geum-myeong] In a season
of unchanging youth,

01:10:19.006 --> 01:10:22.551
my mom still dyed her nails
with crushed balsam flowers.

01:10:23.093 --> 01:10:23.969
Oh.

01:10:25.679 --> 01:10:27.389
You never age, do you?

01:10:29.975 --> 01:10:31.602
What's the big deal with aging?

01:10:31.685 --> 01:10:36.065
Did you feel any different
going from your thirties to your forties?

01:10:36.148 --> 01:10:38.192
You feel the same at your age?

01:10:38.275 --> 01:10:40.110
Oh, exhausting.

01:10:40.945 --> 01:10:42.404
It's the same.

01:10:43.280 --> 01:10:45.699
It's the same.

01:10:47.117 --> 01:10:48.619
You feel the same inside,

01:10:50.579 --> 01:10:52.373
but when you look in the mirror,

01:10:53.457 --> 01:10:55.542
an old woman stares at you.

01:10:56.126 --> 01:10:57.878
That's all aging is.

01:10:57.962 --> 01:11:00.297
Mom. It's here! It's here!

01:11:01.215 --> 01:11:02.758
It wasn't a scam, you see?

01:11:03.259 --> 01:11:04.802
SEAFLOWER PUBLISHERS

01:11:05.386 --> 01:11:07.888
I made it very clear to her
that my sister is successful

01:11:07.972 --> 01:11:09.765
and that I own a franchise.

01:11:09.848 --> 01:11:12.226
I thought the publisher
would charge us more

01:11:12.309 --> 01:11:14.895
just because I wanted to publish
a poem collection so quickly.

01:11:14.979 --> 01:11:16.272
It was very last minute.

01:11:17.022 --> 01:11:19.024
But it wasn't a scam, you see?

01:11:19.984 --> 01:11:22.236
Oh, this is just unbelievable.

01:11:23.862 --> 01:11:26.198
Oh Ae-sun's poem collection.

01:11:27.157 --> 01:11:28.158
[Geum-myeong] Mom,

01:11:29.326 --> 01:11:33.580
I bet Dad is laughing at you now,
isn't he?

01:11:35.291 --> 01:11:37.209
[wistful music playing]

01:11:37.293 --> 01:11:39.378
Huh? Grandma's crying again?

01:11:42.631 --> 01:11:44.091
[sobs happily]

01:11:44.842 --> 01:11:46.635
HERE'S TO ALL YOU'VE BEEN THROUGH

01:11:47.136 --> 01:11:47.970
TRIBUTE

01:11:48.053 --> 01:11:50.556
THE BEAUTIFUL, DREAMLIKE STORY
BROUGHT ME TO TEARS

01:11:50.639 --> 01:11:52.349
"I'M SORRY. THANK YOU. I LOVE YOU"

01:11:52.433 --> 01:11:53.267
EDITOR'S NOTE

01:12:01.859 --> 01:12:06.780
MENTAL AND FINANCIAL COMPETENCE

01:12:10.576 --> 01:12:14.371
So you're here to see the flowers today.
How do you feel about it?

01:12:14.455 --> 01:12:16.874
Well, the flowers
remind me of my first love.

01:12:16.957 --> 01:12:18.042
[reporter] Your first love.

01:12:18.125 --> 01:12:20.419
-[man] Of course, yes.
-[woman] Go live with her, then.

01:12:21.253 --> 01:12:23.505
[man] Hye-ran. No, no. That's dirty.

01:12:29.803 --> 01:12:33.057
[middle-aged Ae-sun] Excuse me, ma'am.
Don't stand there.

01:12:34.099 --> 01:12:36.727
Ma'am, who did you come here to see?

01:12:36.810 --> 01:12:38.937
Well, my mother-in-law
said to pick the pretty lady.

01:12:39.605 --> 01:12:43.025
So which of us would it be? Which one?

01:13:01.210 --> 01:13:03.337
LITTLE PUNK

01:13:05.547 --> 01:13:06.799
THE DAY WE BECAME THE SAME AGE

01:13:06.882 --> 01:13:08.133
I WAS TEN WHEN I LOST MOTHER

01:13:08.217 --> 01:13:10.052
SHE LEFT BEHIND HER THREE CHILDREN AT 29

01:13:10.135 --> 01:13:12.137
WHEN I TURNED 29,
I CRIED LIKE I WAS TEN AGAIN

01:13:33.242 --> 01:13:34.493
[music fades]

01:13:41.542 --> 01:13:42.584
[sobs]

01:13:50.092 --> 01:13:50.926
Hey.

01:13:51.760 --> 01:13:52.886
Are you crying?

01:13:55.973 --> 01:13:56.932
[chuckles]

01:13:57.641 --> 01:13:59.059
Oh, what's happening?

01:14:00.727 --> 01:14:02.354
Why is this making me cry?

01:14:04.314 --> 01:14:05.482
Is it that good?

01:14:06.984 --> 01:14:07.943
It's just

01:14:09.236 --> 01:14:10.070
that I'm…

01:14:11.572 --> 01:14:12.406
I'm…

01:14:16.535 --> 01:14:17.911
How can I say it?

01:14:20.789 --> 01:14:21.748
Proud of her.

01:14:23.083 --> 01:14:24.585
So proud.

01:14:27.546 --> 01:14:29.465
OH AE-SUN

01:14:29.548 --> 01:14:30.382
CONTENTS

01:14:30.466 --> 01:14:32.676
SPRING IN A HEARTBEAT
THE BLAZING SUMMER SUNSHINE

01:14:33.260 --> 01:14:35.804
[Geum-myeong] Should we do something
for your debut publication?

01:14:37.389 --> 01:14:39.766
Can you at least pretend
you want something?

01:14:39.850 --> 01:14:43.812
Your daughter's doing quite well now.
I even bought you your house.

01:14:44.354 --> 01:14:46.231
See me more.

01:14:46.315 --> 01:14:49.359
I want to see my busy daughter at least

01:14:49.443 --> 01:14:52.279
a hundred more times before I go.

01:14:54.573 --> 01:14:56.617
Why would you say that?

01:14:58.327 --> 01:14:59.745
I get to see you

01:15:00.287 --> 01:15:02.456
maybe ten times a year.

01:15:04.458 --> 01:15:07.461
So I'd like to see you
a hundred times a year.

01:15:09.296 --> 01:15:10.255
[moans]

01:15:11.089 --> 01:15:13.342
So you should move to Seoul with me.

01:15:14.051 --> 01:15:16.261
Why do you go to
the nursing home that often?

01:15:18.764 --> 01:15:21.391
You still need a calling in the world.

01:15:21.475 --> 01:15:23.393
It's important at my age.

01:15:23.477 --> 01:15:26.271
I hate being treated
like I'm a waste of space.

01:15:26.855 --> 01:15:29.358
I'd just be relaxing mostly
in that situation.

01:15:30.275 --> 01:15:33.070
You were so, so busy your entire life.

01:15:34.071 --> 01:15:35.364
I only go 'cause

01:15:35.948 --> 01:15:37.616
I get excited doing that.

01:15:39.660 --> 01:15:42.955
See, when I'm there,
"Teacher Ae-sun" is what I'm called.

01:15:43.956 --> 01:15:48.210
Basically, I'm moving up
quite a lot in this world.

01:15:52.714 --> 01:15:56.635
Once, I was a haenyeo's daughter
who cried every day at sea,

01:15:57.219 --> 01:16:01.431
then a bookworm who was so embarrassed
about everything in the world.

01:16:01.515 --> 01:16:04.518
[Ae-sun] We have a house and a boat.

01:16:05.185 --> 01:16:08.605
[middle-aged Ae-sun] Then the most excited
and elated wife of a boat captain.

01:16:11.400 --> 01:16:13.110
Village Chief Oh,

01:16:13.777 --> 01:16:16.613
the fish-filleting lady at the market…

01:16:16.697 --> 01:16:18.156
Crazy, right? And then I was chosen.

01:16:18.240 --> 01:16:20.284
Supposedly a teacher at 70,

01:16:20.367 --> 01:16:22.828
and now, Oh Ae-sun the poet.

01:16:24.121 --> 01:16:27.124
You learn about life
if you live through it.

01:16:28.917 --> 01:16:32.504
How shameful it would've been
if I gave up on life.

01:16:33.255 --> 01:16:36.508
I'm so glad I lived all that I could.

01:16:37.759 --> 01:16:41.680
So… your back in springtime now?

01:16:42.848 --> 01:16:43.682
Mm-hmm.

01:16:44.182 --> 01:16:45.601
It's spring again.

01:16:46.435 --> 01:16:47.269
Um,

01:16:48.770 --> 01:16:50.063
I thought life

01:16:50.147 --> 01:16:53.609
went from spring to summer

01:16:53.692 --> 01:16:55.694
to autumn to winter.

01:16:56.987 --> 01:16:58.030
That's not

01:16:59.906 --> 01:17:01.408
necessarily true.

01:17:01.491 --> 01:17:03.035
Sometimes,

01:17:04.119 --> 01:17:06.663
it's winter, sometimes it's spring.

01:17:10.292 --> 01:17:12.711
I had lots of spring days, dear.

01:17:12.794 --> 01:17:14.588
Many, many of those.

01:17:17.299 --> 01:17:20.802
[Geum-myeong] The countless stars
of her years formed a galaxy.

01:17:21.762 --> 01:17:24.514
[middle-aged Ae-sun]
I've had many wonderful,

01:17:25.932 --> 01:17:27.893
memorable moments.

01:17:30.687 --> 01:17:31.605
[chuckles]

01:17:33.440 --> 01:17:36.026
There's seven years of my life
in the flower fields

01:17:36.109 --> 01:17:37.778
living in this book.

01:17:39.196 --> 01:17:42.157
[Geum-myeong] All the memories
that she kept close to her chest

01:17:42.240 --> 01:17:43.909
were now in full bloom.

01:17:44.409 --> 01:17:45.577
So

01:17:47.037 --> 01:17:47.913
are you happy?

01:17:50.999 --> 01:17:51.833
Mm.

01:17:53.043 --> 01:17:53.919
Oh yes.

01:17:54.878 --> 01:17:56.630
I'm so

01:17:56.713 --> 01:17:58.507
happy, yes.

01:17:59.800 --> 01:18:03.762
[Geum-myeong] My mother's heart sparkled
in the most beautiful colors.

01:18:03.845 --> 01:18:05.847
[emotional music playing]

01:18:06.682 --> 01:18:08.517
[middle-aged Ae-sun] To my love,

01:18:09.851 --> 01:18:12.437
from age nine to now,

01:18:13.438 --> 01:18:14.731
my life

01:18:15.232 --> 01:18:18.276
was always in spring because of you.

01:18:19.027 --> 01:18:20.404
[camera shutter clicks]

01:18:21.029 --> 01:18:23.240
This book wouldn't exist

01:18:23.323 --> 01:18:24.991
if it weren't for you.

01:18:26.743 --> 01:18:28.453
I will live my life

01:18:29.496 --> 01:18:31.957
as though every day is spring

01:18:32.040 --> 01:18:33.583
until we meet again.

01:18:33.667 --> 01:18:34.501
Come here.

01:18:38.130 --> 01:18:40.173
When I grow up to be a poet,

01:18:40.257 --> 01:18:42.300
I'll wear two-piece outfits
like Um Aing-ran.

01:18:42.968 --> 01:18:45.679
And, when I'm rich,
I'll live in a two-story house

01:18:45.762 --> 01:18:47.889
and raise an adorable dog.

01:18:47.973 --> 01:18:51.017
And I'll pay for
piano lessons for our kids.

01:18:51.101 --> 01:18:53.019
I'll go out to eat nearly always.

01:18:53.812 --> 01:18:58.024
Um, then I'll drive Jeeps
and wear Ray-Bans.

01:18:58.525 --> 01:18:59.359
You love cars?

01:19:00.318 --> 01:19:01.278
Yeah.

01:19:01.361 --> 01:19:03.447
[chuckles] I didn't know you liked things.

01:19:03.530 --> 01:19:06.992
I'm gonna take you
and drive that car all over the place.

01:19:07.576 --> 01:19:08.994
I'm going to the States too.

01:19:09.745 --> 01:19:11.371
Love it! [laughs]

01:19:12.581 --> 01:19:15.709
We can go together, chat,
do anything you want.

01:19:15.792 --> 01:19:16.668
Love it.

01:19:17.377 --> 01:19:18.295
I love it too.

01:19:19.546 --> 01:19:22.591
Let's do all kinds of things
all our lives.

01:19:22.674 --> 01:19:24.468
Let's do everything we'd like to.

01:19:24.551 --> 01:19:25.677
[laughs]

01:19:25.761 --> 01:19:27.763
[wistful music playing]

01:19:37.272 --> 01:19:39.816
[Geum-myeong] "To my parents
who were so young

01:19:39.900 --> 01:19:43.361
and always so tender-hearted
all throughout the seasons."

01:19:43.862 --> 01:19:47.616
"With remorse, gratitude,
and the deepest respect,

01:19:47.699 --> 01:19:49.868
thanks for showing us what to do

01:19:51.077 --> 01:19:53.246
when life gives you tangerines."

01:20:09.179 --> 01:20:11.181
[gentle pop music playing]

01:22:49.214 --> 01:22:54.219
"IF YOU CAN'T, JUST BACK DOWN.
WE'RE ALWAYS HERE FOR YOU."

01:23:01.393 --> 01:23:03.269
[music fades]
